WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.532 --> 00:00:05.282
(relaxing music)

00:00:13.092 --> 00:00:15.064
- In the Netherlands, it rains a lot.

00:00:15.064 --> 00:00:18.311
Since I grew up, the
weather is really changing.

00:00:18.311 --> 00:00:21.006
It rains more, it rains more heavy,

00:00:21.006 --> 00:00:23.068
and it's getting warmer as well.

00:00:23.068 --> 00:00:26.924
People have a tendency to
complain about the weather.

00:00:26.924 --> 00:00:29.647
I think it's beautiful
when you hear the rain,

00:00:29.647 --> 00:00:31.294
it really changes pace,

00:00:31.294 --> 00:00:33.458
and it also sustains growth.

00:00:33.458 --> 00:00:37.625
I wanted to make something
to celebrate the weather.

00:00:49.002 --> 00:00:52.252
Made-by-rain started
after I got the heritage

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:53.446
of my grandfather.

00:00:53.446 --> 00:00:55.193
This heritage was a collection

00:00:55.193 --> 00:00:56.722
of calendars

00:00:56.722 --> 00:01:00.057
where he wrote down every
day the weather conditions.

00:01:00.057 --> 00:01:01.837
When I was doing my master's,

00:01:01.837 --> 00:01:05.723
I thinking, how can I
actually map the weather?

00:01:05.723 --> 00:01:08.168
And then I started to doing
the same as my grandfather,

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:09.537
but then with textiles.

00:01:09.537 --> 00:01:12.599
I made this technique,
pluviography,

00:01:12.599 --> 00:01:14.849
which is drawing with rain.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.491
There are two ways to make
made-by-rain textiles.

00:01:23.491 --> 00:01:24.936
One I call analog version,

00:01:24.936 --> 00:01:26.750
and one a digital version.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:29.153
When I'm in The Hague at my studio

00:01:29.153 --> 00:01:30.208
and it starts to rain,

00:01:30.208 --> 00:01:32.086
I go up on the roof,

00:01:32.086 --> 00:01:34.058
and for the analog version,

00:01:34.058 --> 00:01:39.036
I use two layers of textile
and of ink with paper.

00:01:39.036 --> 00:01:41.626
And when the rain hits the surface,

00:01:41.626 --> 00:01:44.091
the paper gets wet,
and it starts to bleed,

00:01:44.091 --> 00:01:46.747
so that makes it, the white
cloth becomes black or blue,

00:01:46.747 --> 00:01:48.592
depending on the color.

00:01:48.592 --> 00:01:53.414
The digital version is
prepared with a layer of ink

00:01:53.414 --> 00:01:54.833
already on the cloth,

00:01:54.833 --> 00:01:59.000
and when the rain hits the
surface, the ink starts to bleed.

00:02:06.023 --> 00:02:07.848
After I put it in the rain,

00:02:07.848 --> 00:02:09.668
I fixate the textiles,

00:02:09.668 --> 00:02:11.884
and then you can wear it.

00:02:11.884 --> 00:02:14.197
With this technique, you
can see every rain drop,

00:02:14.197 --> 00:02:17.197
and every little detail in the rain.

00:02:21.951 --> 00:02:25.185
So after I fixate my textiles,

00:02:25.185 --> 00:02:28.578
I check the data from the weather station,

00:02:28.578 --> 00:02:31.477
in order to really finalize the moment,

00:02:31.477 --> 00:02:35.644
and the data, which is
silk-screened upon the textile.

00:02:36.578 --> 00:02:39.003
With our data comes in statistics,

00:02:39.003 --> 00:02:41.628
and I wanted to make a more visual way

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:43.886
of archiving weather.

00:02:43.886 --> 00:02:46.740
On the textiles, I note the location,

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:50.952
the date, the time interval,
the millimeters of rain,

00:02:50.952 --> 00:02:53.479
and the weather circumstances,

00:02:53.479 --> 00:02:56.664
and I do this because I see
the textiles as documents,

00:02:56.664 --> 00:02:57.876
so they're all unique.

00:02:57.876 --> 00:02:59.977
Five minutes of drizzle is very different

00:02:59.977 --> 00:03:03.070
than five minutes of heavy rainfall.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:06.320
(exciting piano music)

00:03:08.607 --> 00:03:11.134
I've hoped that with the
textiles that I make,

00:03:11.134 --> 00:03:14.619
people get a new awareness of rain,

00:03:14.619 --> 00:03:17.727
and a new relationship
with the environment.

00:03:17.727 --> 00:03:20.548
I hope people see the beauty, as well.

00:03:20.548 --> 00:03:22.504
Not only the pouring rain,

00:03:22.504 --> 00:03:26.671
and waiting for it to be dry
to continue your daily life.

